e_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":6,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":6,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":6,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":6}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":79,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 76 is closed, but its target isn't met. The three replay VIs exist and are wired correctly, but they return empty images, so the M8(b) number check (the same recorded frames through the S1 and S3 copies) can't start yet. No LabVIEW job is left running, and the runner's end hook closes LabVIEW.\n\n**What works now:**\n- **Frames folder:** `G:\\m8_replay_frames\\` holds 10,044 hardlinks to the recorded frames, with a manifest. It uses no extra disk space.\n- **New wiring tool:** `gscript.connect_ctl_ind` wires a front-panel control straight to an indicator. It was tested over 20 calls, and LabVIEW's handle count did not grow.\n- **Pane base VI:** a VI with exactly the connector pane of `IMAQdx Get Image` and no NI library owner. It swaps into the old node's place with all 9 wires kept.\n- **The three replay VIs:** they run, their panes match their sources, and in the frame-grabber copy the only change is `#529`. Their image output is empty, as described below.\n- **`make_default`:** now reports its errors.\n- **Log classifier (76-2, 28 pass / 0 fail):** `tools/logclass.py` now decides whether a log is a build or a review from the command that ran, not the file name. That fixes the cycle-75 retrospective item; 18 existing logs moved from build to review.\n\n**Why the images are empty:** two numbers (the loop count and the 10044 modulus) were stored as saved defaults of panel controls. They were lost at save with no error, so the loop never runs. The exact cause is still open; PD20 moves those numbers to fixed values on the diagram instead.\n\n**Plan changes** (`docs/m8-real-run-plan.md` Pre-decided 16–20):\n- **Missing frames:** the recorded frames are numbered 4–11825 with 124 gaps, so a frame is now picked by position in the sorted list, not by its number.\n- **Frame choice:** the peer review showed that choosing frames by camera buffer number would feed the two VIs different image sequences. Each run starts at a different live buffer, and the tracking step carries values from one frame to the next. Frames are now chosen by call count, and S1 and S3 each run in their own LabVIEW launch.\n- **`Missed frames?`:** the original logic gives TRUE when the camera returns the requested buffer, which is its normal value. The old prediction of False is withdrawn.\n\n**Retrospective** (both findings accepted and written into the review file):\n- **Inference over measurement (22 min, $1.49):** I let a material session choose to hold those numbers as panel defaults, and nothing read them back from the saved file before the tests ran. From now on every such value is read back from disk first. The replay VIs are also rebuilt through a stage script, so the dry-run and prior-art checks apply; this cycle built them as diagnostic scripts, which skipped those checks.\n- **`device-failed` (threshold 1):** `guard_peer` skips `selftest_*.log` by file name, so one failed prediction got no review routing. Fixing it is the next cycle's first act.\n\n**Next (cycle 77):** fix `guard_peer` to decide by command. Then build the tool that puts a constant on a loop's own terminals, rebuild the replay VIs through a stage script, and run the frame tests. Details are in STATUS `## NEXT` and `tools/bench/next.json`.\n\nSTATUS.md is still over 100 lines, and shrinking it is still owed. It still points at the old plan document, which is why the retrospective's out-of-plan check listed every file this cycle.","ttft_ms":2061,"type":"result","duration_ms":8262160,"uuid":"c1eccefd-4896-4d3e-95e5-fb9237fa8585","ttft_str